<title>BELGIUM: Belgian 2007 OLO auctioned at average 5.746 pct. [CORRECTED 13:55 GMT]</title>
<headline>Belgian 2007 OLO auctioned at average 5.746 pct. [CORRECTED 13:55 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian Treasury gave the following details of the outcome of its monthly government bond auction -</p>
<p>6.25 pct, March 28, 2007 OLO</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted (stop) price	    103.65</p>
<p>    Amount allotted				14.175 billion francs</p>
<p>    Percentage taken at stop		  100</p>
<p>    Avg weighted price / yield		103.650 / 5.746 pct</p>
<p>(Corrects to remove line, making clear that nothing was sold on Monday at the non-competitive auction, which takes place on Tuesday)  </p>
<p>8.75 pct, June 25 2002 OLO </p>
<p>    Lowest accepted (stop) price	    117.70</p>
<p>    Amount allotted				 8.03 billion</p>
<p>    Percentage taken at stop		  29.71</p>
<p>    Avg weighted price / yield		117.743 / 4.672 pct</p>
<p>Total amount allotted in both lines:  22.205 billion</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
